---- ALGORITHMS ----
>> C2: Explain how you read and write to the console for the kernel monitor.

To read from the console, I used input_getc, which is defined in
devices/input.h and returns the ASCII code of a single character taken from
stdin. I run input_getc in a loop, accumulating the characters in a buffer and
also copying them to stdout until the user types a return, and then it will
interpret the command that is in the buffer. For all writing to the console, I
used printf, which is defined in lib/stdio.h and works the same way as the
standard libc one does.

